@startuml
title Arc fee routing: current implementation vs. whitepaper target
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #EAF6F0
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
skinparam partition {
  BorderColor #2E8B67
}
|Today (arc-node v0.8.x)|
start
:Transaction pays gas in native USDC\n(EWMA base fee, 20-20,000 gwei bounds);
:reward_beneficiary():\nbase fee + priority fee;
:Credit full amount in USDC\nto proposer's --suggested-fee-recipient;<<#EAF6F0>>
note right: no burn, no conversion,\nno staker share, no issuance
|Whitepaper target (post-PoS)|
:Fee priced in stablecoin,\npaid in USDC, other stables, ARC or future assets;
:Protocol-level conversion to ARC\n"at block settlement";<<#FFF4E0>>
note right: price source\nnot specified
split
  :Distribution:\nvalidator commission,\nremainder to stakers pro rata;
split again
  :Permanent burn\n(ratio set by governance);<<#FDEEEE>>
end split
:Plus inflation-funded ARC issuance\n(decaying from ~2-3%);
stop
@enduml
